1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,978
This is our capstone:

2
00:00:02,028 --> 00:00:07,552
an intelligent dental assistant that reads
a panoramic X-ray, one tooth at a time.

3
00:00:08,952 --> 00:00:14,080
A panoramic X-ray, or OPG, shows
every tooth in one picture.

4
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:16,743
A dentist reads it tooth by tooth.

5
00:00:16,793 --> 00:00:18,232
We automate that reading:

6
00:00:18,282 --> 00:00:23,254
find each tooth, number it with the standard
dental numbering, FDI, and report what

7
00:00:23,304 --> 00:00:24,522
we see.

8
00:00:25,922 --> 00:00:30,492
Our six-stage system takes one X-ray and
returns a report for every tooth, plus

9
00:00:30,542 --> 00:00:35,035
a marked-up picture, in about one point
seven seconds on an ordinary processor with

10
00:00:35,085 --> 00:00:36,833
no graphics card.

11
00:00:36,883 --> 00:00:41,300
Its models hold ninety-five million
learned values, and it runs as a simple web

12
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:42,428
demo.

13
00:00:43,828 --> 00:00:45,528
It is built on public data:

14
00:00:45,578 --> 00:00:50,680
the Tufts set of a thousand X-rays, the
DENTEX challenge set, and the CariesXrays

15
00:00:50,730 --> 00:00:51,815
set.

16
00:00:51,865 --> 00:00:56,793
X-rays from four Ningxia hospitals are kept
aside for testing only, never for training,

17
00:00:56,843 --> 00:01:02,326
and the UFBA-425 set was never seen by
our tooth finder or numbering model.

18
00:01:03,726 --> 00:01:06,115
One question shaped the project.

19
00:01:06,165 --> 00:01:09,865
Caries is most common in
the back teeth, the molars.

20
00:01:09,915 --> 00:01:14,506
So a simple rule that ignores the image,
and always names the same eight molars,

21
00:01:14,556 --> 00:01:18,115
already scores well on the
usual tooth-by-tooth score.

22
00:01:18,165 --> 00:01:21,696
Every result here is compared
with that blind rule.

23
00:01:23,096 --> 00:01:27,616
Now, how it works, following one
real X-ray through every stage.

24
00:01:27,666 --> 00:01:32,398
It is one of the one hundred and sixty-four
DENTEX images we score on, about three

25
00:01:32,448 --> 00:01:35,066
thousand by fifteen hundred pixels.

26
00:01:36,466 --> 00:01:38,681
Stage one finds the teeth.

27
00:01:38,731 --> 00:01:43,007
A detector trained on three datasets
looks at the image rotated ninety degrees,

28
00:01:43,057 --> 00:01:44,725
then maps its boxes back:

29
00:01:44,775 --> 00:01:49,828
thirty-two teeth, every one found with
confidence above zero point seven nine.

30
00:01:51,228 --> 00:01:53,476
Stage two numbers the teeth.

31
00:01:53,526 --> 00:01:57,835
Each tooth is cropped with a margin, and a
second model uses the crop and its position

32
00:01:57,885 --> 00:02:01,161
to predict the tooth's number, its FDI code.

33
00:02:01,211 --> 00:02:04,617
A one-to-one matching step stops
two teeth getting the same number:

34
00:02:04,667 --> 00:02:07,782
thirty-two teeth, thirty-two distinct codes.

35
00:02:09,182 --> 00:02:11,593
Stage three looks for caries.

36
00:02:11,643 --> 00:02:15,658
Another detector finds the decay
itself, across the whole image:

37
00:02:15,708 --> 00:02:17,365
nine boxes.

38
00:02:17,415 --> 00:02:22,544
Each box is assigned to the tooth it
overlaps most, so nine teeth are flagged.

39
00:02:23,944 --> 00:02:28,703
A severity model grades each flagged
tooth as caries or deep caries.

40
00:02:28,753 --> 00:02:31,931
Here, only tooth twenty-one is graded deep.

41
00:02:31,981 --> 00:02:36,529
We retrained this model and tested
it once on X-rays it had never seen.

42
00:02:36,579 --> 00:02:41,181
It scored zero point seven seven, where
one is perfect, against zero point four

43
00:02:41,231 --> 00:02:43,083
eight for a blind rule.

44
00:02:43,133 --> 00:02:48,322
That was on teeth the dentists had marked,
not yet on the teeth our system flags.

45
00:02:49,722 --> 00:02:52,622
Stage four is an abnormality flag.

46
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:56,752
A model looks at a taller crop around each
tooth and flags it when it is close to

47
00:02:56,802 --> 00:02:58,981
something an expert marked as abnormal:

48
00:02:59,031 --> 00:03:02,611
here, teeth eleven,
thirty-seven and forty-eight.

49
00:03:02,661 --> 00:03:07,796
It is not a periodontal, or gum disease,
diagnosis, and its severity grade is switched

50
00:03:07,846 --> 00:03:08,868
off.

51
00:03:10,268 --> 00:03:14,859
Stages five and six combine everything
into one record per tooth, stamped with a

52
00:03:14,909 --> 00:03:18,635
fingerprint, a hash, of
every model that ran.

53
00:03:18,685 --> 00:03:22,958
The overlay shows findings in
orange, and everything else in blue.

54
00:03:24,358 --> 00:03:28,438
Checked against the dentists' annotations,
seven of the nine flags land on teeth

55
00:03:28,488 --> 00:03:31,769
with caries, and four teeth
with caries are missed.

56
00:03:31,819 --> 00:03:35,030
That is one image, shown as an example.

57
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:37,528
The measured numbers come next.

58
00:03:38,928 --> 00:03:39,878
Part three:

59
00:03:39,776 --> 00:03:41,589
results over time.

60
00:03:41,639 --> 00:03:47,502
In August, the system ran end to end, and
was validated on four outside hospitals.

61
00:03:47,552 --> 00:03:49,643
Then came an uncomfortable finding:

62
00:03:49,693 --> 00:03:52,850
the blind rule tied with us, or beat us.

63
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:57,154
On the fourth of September, a new caries
detector became the first method to beat

64
00:03:57,204 --> 00:03:59,850
it, on two of three datasets.

65
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:04,813
On the tenth of October, a
review checked every number.

66
00:04:04,863 --> 00:04:09,107
It found that the bone-loss score of zero
point nine two was too high, because the

67
00:04:09,157 --> 00:04:13,259
X-rays it was checked on were also in
its training data, and that its label was

68
00:04:13,309 --> 00:04:15,908
not really periodontal bone loss.

69
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,487
First, the front end.

70
00:04:20,537 --> 00:04:25,617
A new tooth detector, trained on
several datasets, replaced the old one.

71
00:04:25,667 --> 00:04:30,704
On DENTEX, the share of teeth found rose
from seventy-one to over ninety-nine percent,

72
00:04:30,754 --> 00:04:34,280
and correct numbering from fifty-eight
to ninety-three, though the new detector

73
00:04:34,330 --> 00:04:36,704
had trained on DENTEX.

74
00:04:36,754 --> 00:04:41,791
On the unseen UFBA-425 set, correct
numbering rose from twenty-one to forty-four

75
00:04:41,841 --> 00:04:43,563
and a half percent.

76
00:04:43,613 --> 00:04:44,563
The cost:

77
00:04:44,385 --> 00:04:49,660
box accuracy on Tufts fell from zero
point seven two to zero point five nine.

78
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:55,923
For caries, our system's score rose from
zero point three eight to zero point five,

79
00:04:55,973 --> 00:04:58,619
against zero point three
two for the blind rule:

80
00:04:58,669 --> 00:05:02,558
a lead of nearly eighteen
points, too large to be chance.

81
00:05:02,608 --> 00:05:07,449
Across the four Ningxia hospitals, agreement
with the dentists' marks reached sixty-eight

82
00:05:07,499 --> 00:05:10,686
percent, nine points above the blind rule.

83
00:05:12,086 --> 00:05:16,584
Stage four went the other way,
because its old score was inflated.

84
00:05:16,634 --> 00:05:21,051
On X-rays it had never seen, the original
model found seven point six percent of

85
00:05:21,101 --> 00:05:24,008
the teeth it should flag, not eighty-three.

86
00:05:24,058 --> 00:05:28,443
Retrained properly, it finds twenty-seven
and a half percent, while staying right

87
00:05:28,493 --> 00:05:32,856
on ninety-six percent of normal teeth,
and eleven to twenty-seven percent across

88
00:05:32,906 --> 00:05:34,725
three training runs.

89
00:05:34,775 --> 00:05:38,116
Its severity model had
learned image contrast.

90
00:05:38,166 --> 00:05:42,475
Retrained on the right labels, it did no
better than a simple position rule, so

91
00:05:42,525 --> 00:05:44,648
its grade stays withheld.

92
00:05:46,048 --> 00:05:49,035
Behind every number is a saved file.

93
00:05:49,085 --> 00:05:52,676
Automatically checked claims in the paper
went from one hundred twenty-seven to

94
00:05:52,726 --> 00:05:57,187
two hundred fifteen, tests from one
seventy-four to two hundred fourteen, and every

95
00:05:57,237 --> 00:06:01,282
default model is checked against
its fingerprint before it loads.

96
00:06:02,682 --> 00:06:06,730
So the review lowered the numbers that were
too high, raised the ones a better tooth

97
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:11,076
detector earned, and named every
stage for what it really measures.

98
00:06:12,476 --> 00:06:13,426
Next:

99
00:06:13,172 --> 00:06:17,393
a six-page conference paper, built from
these checked numbers, and choosing the

100
00:06:17,443 --> 00:06:19,300
venue with our mentor.

101
00:06:19,350 --> 00:06:20,678
Thank you.
